{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]The Passover was over and [Eb]the caravans went [Bb]home
Mary thought he walked with cou[Eb]sins, Joseph thought he'd gone on
A [Bb]day out on the road [Eb]they searched among the friends
But he [Bb]was nowhere to be found when the [Eb]day came to its end
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]After three days they [Eb]found him in the temple
[Bb]Sitting among the teachers
[F/A]Listening to them and asking them [Eb]questions
[F]Everyone who heard him was astound[Bb]ed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Why were you [F/A]searching for [Gm]me
Did you [Eb]not know that I must be in my [F]Father's house
[Bb]Why were you [F/A]searching for [Gm]me
I [Eb]must be in my [F]Father's [Bb]house [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Child, why have you done this to us, his [Eb]mother said in tears
Your [Bb]father and I have been searching for [Eb]you in anguish
He [Bb]went down with them to Nazareth and con[Eb]tinued to obey them
And his [Bb]mother treasured all these [Eb]things in her heart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Why were you [F/A]searching for [Gm]me
Did you [Eb]not know that I must be in my [F]Father's house
